THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
The proposal's skeptical combination (intersection of label sets across contexts) is incompatible with the demand to preserve reinstatement as a derived property. In standard argumentation semantics, reinstatement says a non-defeated argument is always accepted, but under an intersection-of-contexts skeptical rule, a root r that is valid in context C1 yet attacked in a different context C2 will be excluded from the intersection whenever C2's local environment happens to be unfavorable. r thus fails to be reinstated even when no globally committed root refutes it; reinstatement becomes a merely context-local accident rather than a derived property of the combined extension. Since the problem context requires reinstatement to be preserved, this is a substantive fault.

TARGET:
Reframe commitment as case-relative: each committed root is associated with a set of contextual assumptions, and the extension is the set of nodes accepted in at least one context, with a skeptical combination (e.g., intersection of label sets across contexts). This extends SRC_008 into a multi-context framework. Criticizable: may lead to exponential contexts; determinism may be lost unless contexts are totally ordered.